## VERDICT: PASS

**Risk Grade**: L1

No violation mandating rejection was found.

## Mode note, stated because the auditor is also the author

`audit_risk_score` returned `option_b_required: false`. Independent review was
**not** dispatched for this pass, and the justification is recorded rather than
assumed.

This design lineage has already had five independent review cycles: a continuing
reviewer across fifteen authoring iterations of the blocking design, and four
fresh-context architectural reviews. The most recent returned three blocking
findings against this very plan -- an advisory control that could block through
override friction, an unguarded control whose callees raise, and a consequent
break in an existing test -- all of which are fixed in the artifact under audit.

A sixth review has low marginal value against a 486-line plan whose design is now
well characterised, and the operator has observed that the cycle is generating
findings faster than it closes work. That observation is itself evidence about
where the marginal value lies.

The countervailing risk is real and is named: SG-007 author-momentum applies, the
author wrote this plan, and a solo audit is the weaker instrument. The mitigation
is that every binding pass below was executed rather than reasoned about, and one
finding was caught and corrected mid-audit (see Pre-verdict correction).

